<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-S.Australia sees lower 1996/97 grain harvest.</title>
<headline>RTRS-S.Australia sees lower 1996/97 grain harvest.</headline>
<dateline>ADELAIDE 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Graingrowers in South Australia, Australia's main barley growing state, were expecting a very good 1996/97 harvest, with an estimated total 5.3 million tonnes, the State's Primary Industries department said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Senior agronomist Steven Hogg told Reuters the harvest was expected to be slightly down on 1995/96's record 5.5 million tonnes due mainly to the late start to the season.</p>
<p>Hogg said the wheat harvest was estimated to be 2.6 million tonnes, down on last year's 2.9 million tonnes but up on the five year average of 2.3 million tonnes.</p>
</text>
